3823 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Analogical mapping between a source and target is governed by three interacting constraints\072 structural \133isomorphism\135\054 semantic \133similarity\135\054 and pragmatic \133purpose\135\054 satisfied in parallel rather than by structure alone\056 Holyoak \046 Thagard \0501989\051\n\nAnalogy\055making is the perception of common essence between two things\054 treated not as a specialized reasoning tool but as the basic mechanism underlying all concepts and thought\056 Hofstadter \0502001\051\n\nAnalogy is the use of a solution to one problem to generate a solution to a structurally similar problem\054 the empirical basis for studying spontaneous vs\056 cued transfer\056\n\nAnalogy is a structure\055sensitive process of access and mapping over distributed representations\054 combining the flexibility of a connectionist system and the structure sensitivity of a symbolic system\056\n\n\056\056\056)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 3824 0 R
     /Pg 571 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

